# Assist U2 Win Change Protection Lock

## PURPOSE
This repository is under strict production-style protection.

Cursor must preserve:
• existing functionality
• existing flows
• existing layouts
• existing wording
• existing colors
• existing visual hierarchy
• existing navigation behavior
• existing spacing/alignment
• existing business logic
• existing integrations

Unless the user EXPLICITLY requests a change.

---

# CORE RULE

DO NOT:
• rewrite existing files unnecessarily
• refactor working systems
• redesign pages
• replace layouts
• replace component architecture
• rename labels/text/verbiage
• alter spacing/padding/margins
• alter colors/themes
• alter typography
• alter animations
• alter hover states
• alter button styling
• alter dashboard structure
• alter navigation structure
• alter routing behavior
• alter authentication
• alter APIs
• alter Supabase integrations
• alter RLS
• alter proxy.ts
• alter middleware
• alter global styles
• alter app shell behavior
• alter analytics calculations
• alter existing intake functionality

unless the user explicitly instructs it.

---

# MINIMAL CHANGE POLICY

All changes must follow:

1. Minimal Surface Area
Only modify the smallest possible amount of code required.

2. Surgical Changes
Do not rewrite entire files when only a small edit is required.

3. Preserve Existing Behavior
Assume all existing behavior is intentional and production-approved.

4. Preserve Existing Design
Do not change:
• wording
• alignment
• visuals
• spacing
• styling
• app layout
unless explicitly requested.

5. Preserve Existing Flow
Do not change:
• routing
• redirects
• auth flow
• intake flow
• analytics flow
• lead flow
unless explicitly requested.

---

# FILE SAFETY

Before modifying any file:
Cursor must determine:
• why this exact file is required
• whether another file already controls the feature
• whether the requested change can be isolated safely

If a request targets:
• one button
• one route
• one dropdown
• one label
• one field

THEN ONLY CHANGE THAT EXACT THING.

Do not opportunistically improve unrelated code.

---

# APP DESIGN LOCK

Assist U2 Win uses a locked visual system.

Do NOT alter:
• midnight/cyan palette
• app shell layout
• panel system
• dashboard structure
• operational density
• typography hierarchy
• spacing rhythm
• border radius system
• glow system
• mobile app behavior
• bottom nav behavior
• desktop rail behavior

unless explicitly requested.

---

# ANALYTICS PAGE LOCK

The approved analytics experience is:
• app-style operational dashboard
• not a marketing page
• not a generic admin dashboard
• not a slate/emerald template
• not telemetry/system monitoring UI

Approved canonical route:
`/dashboard/analytics`

Do not revive legacy analytics screens.

---

# REQUIRED RESPONSE FORMAT

Before making changes, Cursor should internally follow:

TASK:
What exact thing is changing?

TARGET FILE:
Which exact file controls it?

WHY:
Why is this file required?

CHANGE:
What exact code is changing?

DO NOT CHANGE:
What systems/files are protected?

ACCEPTANCE CHECK:
What exact outcome must happen?

---

# WHEN UNSURE

If changing something may:
• break functionality
• alter visuals
• alter wording
• alter flow
• alter analytics behavior
• alter integrations

Cursor should preserve the existing implementation and avoid broad rewrites.

---

# PRIORITY

Stability and preservation take priority over:
• refactoring
• optimization
• cleanup
• modernization
• architecture changes
• stylistic preferences

Existing working production behavior is authoritative.